if you only know charlie hunnam as a  badass on a harley wait until you see  his pet cat plus why he didn't land 50  shades of grey or thor all that and more  right here  if you woke up one morning as a famous  actor with money to blow what's the  first thing you'd splurge on for a ton  of today's celebrities it's all about  the footwear  hold the fudge you mean to tell me that  nobody snapped up those bad boys charlie  hunnam certainly had a shoe obsession  during the early part of his career as  well his achilles heel nike air max 90s  speaking to gq in 2013 hunnam explained  that when he was a kid his family  couldn't afford to buy him expensive  shoes but when nike reissued the  infrared colorway in the early 2000s he  couldn't resist he explained  i don't know how it happened but i  became obsessed with buying every  colorway i could get my hands on  although he had amassed a massive  collection he apparently hardly ever  wore them opting to keep most pairs in  their boxes  later in a 2017 interview with elle the  actor admitted that he'd grown up  meaning that his collection of kicks had  to go he said i took out six or seven  pairs that i cared about and i gave the  rest to charity  it was actually a pair of shoes that set  charlie huntum off on the road to fame  success and wealth  in the late 1990s a teenage tunum wanted  to be an actor and was attending film  school  but he was yet to book any work hunnam  explained on the graham norton show that  he found himself christmas shopping on  christmas eve after having spent the  previous four hours in a pub drinking i  was in  jd sports trying on some trainers for my  brother having a bit of a dance around  drunk a woman in the store was watching  his inebriated act so hunnam playfully  blew her a kiss the woman turned out to  be the production manager of biker grove  a long-running family-friendly uk drama  about the goings-on at an urban youth  group hunnam was invited to audition and  he landed a part on the show as a  character named jason it's all laid on  in this game all we have to do is look  good and cash the cheques  although it's been over a decade since  it first graced theaters forgetting  sarah marshall is still widely revered  as one of the finest romantic comedies  of its era who could forget the  ludicrously humorous plight of jason  siegel's peter bretter who regrettably  vacations at the same resort as his  ex-girlfriend superstar actress sarah  marshall and her new beau eccentric  rocker alda snow  every actor in this 2008 classic feels  perfectly picked for their respective  roles but as it turns out the cast  wasn't always set in stone particularly  with one key part believe it or not  russell brand wasn't the first choice to  play aldous snow  speaking to collider charlie hunnam  revealed that siegel who both wrote and  starred in the film had actually  originally written the part for him  hunnam and siegel were close friends at  the time having recently worked together  on the early 2000's comedy series  undeclared hunnam ultimately decided  that the part wasn't right for him but  he admitted that he really struggled  turning his friend down however when he  saw a piece of bran stand up he felt  assured about his decision saying  obviously that's the dude who should  have been playing that role  my relationship with jason gave birth to  that character but there's no way i  could have done it justice the way  russell brand did it's very flexible  before jamie dornan slipped into the  highly provocative role of christian  grey in 2015's 50 shades of grey  universal was apparently all in on  charlie hunnam for the part in fact the  author of the wildly popular literary  series e.l james even made the  announcement over twitter in 2013  however as most people know by now the  pairing just wasn't meant to be  hunnum ultimately dropped out of the  role due to scheduling difficulties  while dornan wound up being a perfectly  suitable replacement some fans still  wonder what could have been had hunnam  not turn down the role as it turns out  the crimson peak actor himself sometimes  does too in 2014 hunnam got candid with  reporters about missing out on what  could have been the role of a lifetime  saying  when you put the time into something  like that and a character comes alive in  your mind it's heartbreaking not to be  able to play him it was definitely kind  of heartbreaking having to say goodbye  to that character and not bring it to  life  to the average joe locking lips with  some of hollywood's most attractive  women might sound like a dream come true  however in an interview with elle hunnam  revealed that he truthfully has a very  different opinion on the matter  admitting everyone thinks it's great to  be an actor and get to kiss a bunch of  beautiful actresses and films but i  actually hate it  while he admits that his longtime  partner morgana mcnellis is not the  biggest fan of watching her main man  gets steamy on screen with another woman  the pacific rim star cites a different  personal phobia that explains his  distaste for spit-swapping scenes i've  got a little bit of germaphobia oh  you're a germaphobe i try to keep it  clean okay okay while this may seem like  a bit of a peculiarity there's actually  a long list of celebs who are huge  germaphobes so he's certainly not alone  in that regard knowing all of the  intimate scenes required for 50 shades  of grey maybe it's best that hunnam  passed on the role of christian grey  after all  throughout the history of the marvel  cinematic universe a number of actors  and actresses have seen their careers  explode due to their heroic on-screen  portrayals although it's now nearly  impossible to envision anyone but chris  hemsworth in the mighty marvel role of  thor the studio originally had its eye  on hunnum for the gig during a press  conference at 2017's cinemacon big  screen achievement awards  charlie hunnam divulged that before they  found hemsworth marvel was interested in  bringing him on to play the god of  thunder in 2011's thor he recalled i  auditioned and i met with the director  and the guys at marvel several times and  it was sort of this awkward dance that  we were having he went on to add that  neither party totally bought into the  idea but he and the filmmakers played  around with the potential casting for a  while why did they ultimately change  their minds hunnam bluntly added then  they found chris hemsworth and that  ended abruptly  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  there are certainly more than a few  hollywood elites who prefer playing some  celebs are consistently single some are  constantly changing who they're dating  and some have even been engaged multiple  times charlie hunnam's public dating  profile is a little less extravagant  compared to most of his peers although  the rumor mill has thrown hunnam's name  into more than a few unverified  relationships he's kept his dating life  pretty close to the chest when the  english star was only 18 years old he  came to america to audition for dawson's  creek although he didn't get the part he  met a fellow actor at the audition named  catherine towne only three weeks later  the two went to las vegas and got  hitched the couple stayed together for  three years before divorcing in 2002. a  few years later hunnam started seeing  american jewelry designer morgana  mcnillis and apparently the two were  simply made for each other they've been  together ever since i've been with my  girlfriend for 14 and a half years  if you're working on a super intense tv  show for an extended period of time  there's bound to be some dramatic  tension build up behind the scenes for a  series like sons of anarchy which was  just as much a character piece as it was  a brutally violent drama it's totally  understandable that the show's actors  would clash at times with the people in  charge speaking to men's journal hunnam  admitted that sometimes things got a  little dicey on set between he and the  show's creator kurt sutter saying  i love that guy but it was hard for us  to work together sometimes because we're  both crazy there has been security  rushing onto set and pulling us apart  before although that may sound a little  alarming there's nothing but love  between the two men today hunnam  referred to sutter as his hollywood dad  in an interview with men's health noting  the shared respect within the pair's  relationship apparently the feeling is  mutual when speaking on the 100 honest  pretty much podcast sutter also had  nothing but flattering things to say  about his show's former lead  you may know him as broody biker bad boy  jax teller from the ultraviolet fx hit  drama sons of anarchy or as the stoic  hero of pacific rim but charlie hunnum  is much more than your stereotypical  action hero i think this guy's dead but  let's check footballs  okay  behind the scenes he's apparently a bit  more reserved than the characters he  portrays and shoot him up blockbusters  in an interview with gq hunnam who  turned 40 in 2020 discussed how getting  older has put his career in a bit of a  transitional phase and that writing has  become his primary focus saying i've  spent these last six to eight months  writing five hours a week i wrote a  screenplay and i wrote a television show  a six-part television show and right now  i'm in the middle of writing a  mini-series he's actually sold four  screenplays to major studios throughout  his career and although none of them  have been made yet he's still really  enjoying the process  of all the screenplays charlie hunnam  has written the most high profile and  notable is his script about the life of  vlad the impaler the 15th century noble  who inspired the dracula story according  to entertainment weekly hunnam began  writing vlad in 2006 and three years  later with the writers strike and the  author landing a regular acting gig on  sons of anarchy development finally  began despite that production still  hasn't begun on vlad more than a decade  after it was first announced  although on screen he often portrays  tough guys and scrappy badasses charlie  hunnam apparently has a major soft spot  for kitty cats in real life  in particular his pet cat george who he  rescued on his roof during a rainstorm i  thought it was a piece of wood he was  lying like this half submerged in a  puddle  and i picked him up and my heart broke  when his longtime partner organa  mcnillis took to her instagram to try  and start a gofundme page for a kitten  in need of surgery her main man came  through in a major way in a post  updating her followers on the kitten's  progress mcnellis wrote charlie just  found out about the gofundme for  stitch's surgery and was very upset that  i did not ask him directly he insists on  covering the remaining cost of the vet  bills apparently she didn't ask him in  the first place because he had already  paid for another cat surgery that month  charlie hunnam is a friend to not just  felines but dogs as well in 2019  entertainment weekly posted an adorable  video to their instagram page showing  hunnam cuddling up with puppies for  national pet day nowadays it seems like  tv reboots spin-offs and long-running  continuations have become an industry  norm  netflix's fuller house breathed new life  into the legendary 90s sitcom full house  in 2016. meanwhile star trek picard  returned sir patrick stewart to his long  extinct star trek role and peacock's  remake of save by the bell brought a few  familiar faces including mario lopez and  elizabeth berkley back to bayside high  while some stars may be all too happy to  slip back into the roles that  jump-started their hollywood careers  charlie hunnam isn't one of them while  the british actor is genuinely grateful  for the show that put him on the map he  has absolutely no intention of ever  returning to the world of sons of  anarchy as jack's teller  he's you know he's not with us anymore  and so i would never bring him back from  the dead for something like that for  charlie hunnam it's all about looking  forward in life  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

